out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two counts and the band.** **How many lines in each list cost the writer anything?** **One, on average, and three lists of five gave up nothing** — **and those three are read aloud, because a list that costs nothing is audible in a line and a half.** **Then: who is the person whose work this changes?** **Seven of ten lists had no line about them, and four writers could not name the person without looking it up.**'));

// ===================== 22.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('22.5  Why you, and no adjectives'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open, and strike every adjective as it is said. ⚠ **Eight of ten answered with a claim about themselves and the average was four adjectives in the first sentence.** **What is left of the ten answers goes on the board, and in three cases that was nothing at all** — **which is the cycle, and three minutes of visible blankness teaches it better than any explanation.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Occasions a reader can check: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **A report with a date that the reader has read, and work done with the writer\'s own hands.** **1, 3 and 5 are claims** — **_a good understanding_, _well placed_, _probably the best person_** — **and each invites a comparison with somebody the reader has known for years.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The occasion that looks junior is the one that works, and five writers in this class had removed exactly that sentence.** **Two months of clerical cover is why the central figure of the whole proposal is the writer\'s own and not hearsay** — **and a reader who knows the writer has done the work does not have to decide whether he has understood it.** **Ask the room, after Stage 4b, who removed work they had done with their own hands, and why** — **and all five answers in this class were the same answer, which is that it looked junior.** ⚠ **That is the sentence to leave on the board: _it looked junior_.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The conjunction is the hardest sentence in the unit and the room will not write it unprompted, so require it.** **_The write-off analysis would be better done by Mrs Mouawad, who found nineteen duplicates I had missed in forty minutes, and the table work could be done by the systems manager; the reason I am asking is that I have done both._** **It names two people who could do part of it better, with a figure attached to one of them.** ⚠ **A writer who does that has stopped competing and started describing an overlap, and an overlap is a fact about the work** — **where _best placed_ is a claim the reader has to adjudicate between a stranger and somebody he has known for nine years.** **Nobody wins that adjudication.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _I wrote the re-routing report of 14 March, which you have read._   **2** _I can name the field in the movements table that duplicates._   **3** ⚠ _I did the reconciliation myself for two months in 2024._   **4** **Two people who could do part of it better, with a conjunction.**   **5** ⚠ **Two limits, both findable** — **and when a limit and a soft figure point at the same thing, the document has been checked by its own writer.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
