out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Ms Huda asked why Mr Attar and not somebody else, and three occasions and no adjectives, on four lines of page 3: he wrote the re-routing report of 14 March, which the reader has read; he has read the depot system\'s table structure and can name the three tables and the field that duplicates; and he did the reconciliation himself for two months in 2024 while Mrs Lattouf was on leave. Ms Huda asked what was in the first draft, and that he has a good understanding of the systems and is well placed to look at this, thirteen words with four claims about himself and nothing a reader can do anything with, because Mr Zeidan would have to decide whether to believe him, which is not a decision anybody makes in favour of a stranger. Mrs Oueidat asked why an adjective fails, and Mrs Khoury said because it invites a comparison the reader cannot make and the writer cannot win, since I am thorough asks whether he is more thorough than the systems manager, whom the reader has known for nine years. Dr Qabbani asked about the two months of reconciliation, and that is the occasion that does the most work and he nearly left it out because it is clerical cover and looked junior, and it is the reason the four days is his own figure and not hearsay. Mrs Tarabishi asked whether the answer names anybody else, and it names two people, which is the sentence Mrs Khoury made him write: the write-off analysis would be better done by Mrs Mouawad and the table work by the systems manager, and the reason he is asking is that he has done both the reconciliation and the table structure, which is a conjunction and not a comparison. Mrs Khoury said that is the credible form of why you, because a writer who names two people who could do part of it better has stopped competing and started describing an overlap. Mr Shihabi asked about the limits, and two lines, which are 21.4 arriving in a proposal: he has never worked in a depot and has never taken part in a stock count, and the second is the limit that matters because the fourth of his four sums is about the stock count. Mr Tayara said that weakens the fourth sum, and Mrs Khoury said it labels it, and the two labels agree. Mrs Rizk asked how long the whole answer is, and six lines on page 3, with no adjective about him anywhere in the three pages. Mrs Ajouz asked about the twelve, and twelve adjectives in three pages, eleven of them about himself. And Mr Attar said the thing he will take away is the search: he took each adjective out and wrote in its place the occasion it had been standing in for, and in seven cases there was no occasion at all.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The search is the method and the arithmetic of it is the finding.** **Eleven adjectives about himself, taken out one at a time, each replaced by the occasion it had been standing in for** — **and in seven of the eleven there was no occasion at all.** **That is a measurement of a draft and not a judgement of a person, and the room should be asked to do the same count on their own.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **An adjective about the writer** → **an average of nine a draft; a record of nineteen.**   **2** **The junior occasion removed** → **five of ten.**   **3** ⚠ **No conjunction naming anybody else** → **the room will not write it unprompted.**   **4** **A comparison instead of an overlap** → **_best placed_ cannot be adjudicated in a stranger\'s favour.**   **5** ⚠ **A limit used as modesty** → **a limit is evidence, and it must be relevant.**   **6** **An occasion that makes the reader the person who was wrong** → **see the model\'s last paragraph.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **_I did the reconciliation myself for two months in 2024, while Mrs Lattouf was on leave._** **It looked junior to him and it does the most work** — **because the four days a month in his first paragraph is his own figure and not something he was told, so the reader does not have to decide whether he has understood the work.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **_The write-off analysis would be better done by Mrs Mouawad, who found nineteen duplicates I had missed in forty minutes, and the table work could be done by the systems manager._** **He names the stock controller and the systems manager** — **and the reason he is asking is the conjunction: he has done both the reconciliation and the table structure, and neither of them has done both.**'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **One adjective at a time into the search box, out, and in its place the occasion it had been standing in for.** **In seven of the eleven there was no occasion at all** — **so his first draft made seven claims about himself with nothing underneath them, and the seven are not in the document now.**'));
